Structured Programming Language for 6502/65c02 (8-bit) and
68000 (32-bit) microprocessors

This is a structured programming language for the 8-bit 6502/6510/65c02
microprocessor from the late 1970's and 1980's as used in many home computers
from that era. It also supports the 32-bit Motorola 68000 CPU, for which the
Commodore Amiga is the intended machine. It is a medium to low level programming
language, which aims to provide many conveniences over raw assembly code (even
when using a macro assembler).
